David Damerell schrieb:
> begin  quoting  Klaus Kassner  <Klaus.Kassner@physik.uni-magdeburg.de>:
> 
>>However, I believe there should either be a way to create an - 
>>unattended - altar or there should be at least one guaranteed unattended 
>>altar in each game well above Orcus. 
> 
> 
> Why unattended? Offing the priest only takes moderate thought.

Well, for one thing, I don't like to kill priests as a lawful or neutral 
character.  But if it were a guaranteed altar, I wouldn't mind too much 
whether it would be attended or unattended.  If I needed one of my 
alignment, I'd have to forgo the possibility of donating to that 
particular priest...  (I assume we are in early game, and I need an 
altar more than protection...)

On the other hand, when introducing some ritual to create an altar, I 
think that making it with a priest should involve something more 
powerful, too powerful to be possible in normal circumstances for a weak 
character.  To create an unattended altar should not be *too* difficult. 
  After all, in the Christian religion, protestant branch, anybody can 
make an altar by declaration (as anybody has the right to offer the last 
anointing).  (The catholics are more rigorous about these things :-).) 
In heathen religions, I think a barbarian might also set up an altar to 
his deity just by putting up a few stones in appropriate order. 
(Success might depend on his clerical education...)
